## P0 — LLM-Free Answer Engine (Phase 4 of master plan)

🔴 `reminiscence/evidence/answer_engine.py`
   - `DeterministicAnswerer` handling per-intent structured answers:
     FACT (evidence-backed extractive reply), TEMPORAL/TIMELINE
     (chronologically sorted events), SOURCE_LOOKUP (document/page/section
     list), ENTITY_PROFILE (places/events/people/dates/sources),
     COMPARISON, CROSS_SOURCE (graph paths + supporting sources).
   - Structured output types: FACT | TIMELINE | TABLE | SOURCE_LIST |
     ENTITY_PROFILE | EVENT_LIST | COMPARISON | EXTRACTIVE_SUMMARY.
   - Default wiring in `ReminiscenceEngine.ask()`; LLM only if
     `REMINISCENCE_ENABLE_LLM=true` AND model verified loaded.
   - Acceptance: every supported query class answers with LLM disabled;
     refusal message exactly when evidence insufficient; conflicts surfaced.

🔴 `reminiscence/evidence/context.py` — `EvidencePack`
   (query, evidence_items, entities, temporal_context, provenance,
    conflicts, confidence) with token/char budget management.

🔴 Conflict detection — `Conflict(event_ids, source_ids, conflict_type,
   severity)`; same-entity different date/location detection; never silently
   resolve.

🔴 Explainable confidence model (documented formula):
   confidence = f(evidence_quality × retrieval_strength ×
                  entity_resolution_confidence × temporal_confidence)
   exposed as factors, not a single opaque number.

## P1 — Query Understanding Without an LLM

🟡 Extend `retrieval/query_classifier.py`:
   - New intents: ENTITY_LOOKUP, TIMELINE, COMPARISON (rule-based).
   - Intent-specific weight profiles applied in HybridRetriever
     (FACT→lexical+semantic; TEMPORAL→temporal-heavy; ENTITY→entity+graph; …).
🔴 `retrieval/temporal_parser.py` — dedicated TemporalConstraint parser:
   yesterday/today/last week/month/year, "last Christmas", "in March",
   "between June and August", "before 2024", "after January", "during X";
   relations BEFORE/AFTER/DURING/BETWEEN/OVERLAPS/SAME_DAY/MONTH/YEAR;
   precision + confidence fields.
🔴 `memory/entities.py` — typed extracted entities
   (PERSON/PLACE/ORGANIZATION/DATE/TIME/EVENT/TOPIC/OBJECT/DOCUMENT) with
   surface_form/confidence/source_event_id on MemoryEvent.entities field.
🔴 `graph/resolver.py` — entity resolution pipeline: normalize → exact →
   case-insensitive → alias → fuzzy → embedding similarity → context;
   low-confidence merges require manual confirmation.

## P2 — Memory Graph Service (Phase E)

🟡 Tables exist; service layer missing.
🔴 `graph/service.py`, `graph/traversal.py` — typed edges (MENTIONS,
   OCCURRED_AT, PART_OF, ABOUT, DERIVED_FROM, PARTICIPATED_IN, RELATED_TO,
   SAME_TOPIC, SAME_PERSON, SAME_EVENT, PRECEDES, FOLLOWS), 1/2/3-hop
   traversal with depth caps + explosion guard, provenance per edge
   (confidence/method/model_version/evidence_id), "why selected" explanation.
🔴 People: opt-in face detection → embedding → clustering → candidate →
   user confirmation. No silent biometric identity assertion.
🔴 Places: EXIF GPS → lat/lon/accuracy/city/country/place_id distinct from
   image Region; offline geocoding optional later.

## P3 — Multimodal Production Backends (Phase D)

🟡 ASR: adapter + honest states done; real ONNX Whisper decode path needs
   full segment timestamps + language + confidence end-to-end test with a
   local fixture once artifact installed.
🟡 OCR: abstraction done; production backend selection wired to Model
   Manager manifests; region/confidence output tested synthetically.
🔴 Video intelligence: scene/shot segmentation, duplicate-frame suppression,
   transcript↔keyframe alignment tests, subtitle extraction.
🟡 Image metadata: EXIF capture time done; GPS + visual embeddings pending.

## P4 — Extractive Summarization (no generation)

🔴 `memory/summarizer.py` — TextRank/LexRank/MMR over sentence segments;
   scores = query relevance + entity + temporal + centrality + source
   confidence; selects ONLY existing source text.

## P5 — Reliability / Product (Phases 7–8)

🔴 Backup/restore: manifest.json + checksums + schema/pipeline/embedding
   versions; validate-before-replace restore.
🔴 Secure deletion verification: `verify_deleted(source_id)` proving absence
   across FTS/vector/graph/timeline/evidence/cache.
🔴 PySide6 UI (Phase 6): shell, dashboard, import, search, ask, timeline,
   memory detail, evidence panel, people, places, jobs, settings. UI holds
   zero business logic; all heavy work off-thread via JobQueue.
🔴 CLI parity: `people`, `places`, `backup`, `restore` commands added.

## P6 — Evaluation (Phase 8)

🔴 `benchmarks/retrieval/` curated dataset (documents/images/transcripts/
   temporal/entities/cross-source) with expected event IDs; metrics beyond
   Recall/Precision/MRR: nDCG@K, HitRate@K, temporal accuracy, evidence
   coverage, answer-support rate, source-resolution accuracy. Weights tuned
   against measurements, never hand-set as optimal.

## P7 — Snapdragon/QNN (Phase 9) — HARDWARE-BLOCKED

✅ provider detection, honest routing, CPU-fallback labeling, benchmark
   traceability columns.
🔴 Requires actual Snapdragon HP hardware: QNN model validation, NPU vs CPU
   latency/throughput/memory/thermal/power benchmarks. Until measured: NO
   acceleration claims anywhere.

## Explicit non-goals (per master prompt §DO NOT)

- No rewrite of working core modules.
- No premature vector-DB dependency (NumPy index behind interface is fine).
- No LLM hidden dependency; `REMINISCENCE_ENABLE_LLM=false` must remain a
  fully functional product configuration.
- No cloud mandatory paths, no auto model downloads, no raw-content logging.
